{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetJoWyf6jYz6ibyLBqhZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have enough information. Let me now summarize my findings and move to design.\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nImplement a POST endpoint to confirm shipments that are in CREATED status, moving them to CONFIRMED status while ensuring idempotency and rejecting invalid states.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` - Existing POST /shipments endpoint with create logic\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` - Shipment model and ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-22` - InMemoryShipmentRepository with save() and findById() methods\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` - ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` - ErrorCode enum (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` - Centralized exception handling\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Endpoints throw ApiException subclasses with ErrorCode and message\n- ResourceNotFoundException for 404 responses  \n- ConflictException for 409 responses\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions and status matchers\n- Repository is injected via constructor\n- Responses use ResponseEntity with appropriate HttpStatus\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - Need to add SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED error code (the ticket requires rejecting cancelled shipments with 409, needs a distinct error code)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - Need to add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Need to add tests for all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED idempotency, CANCELLED rejection, 404 not found)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding new ErrorCode to the closed enum might affect clients, but this is necessary for proper error semantics\n- Idempotency requirement means the service must handle repeated confirms safely\n\n**Open questions:** None identified that would block implementation.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the ErrorCode enum. This error code will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in CANCELLED status.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Find shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED; throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED (409)\n   - If status is CREATED; update to CONFIRMED, save, and return\n   - If status is CONFIRMED; return unchanged (idempotent)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` - CREATED → CONFIRMED\n   - `idempotently confirms an already confirmed shipment` - CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (no change)\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with conflict` - CANCELLED → 409 error\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with not found` - 404 error\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- **Alternative**: Use a service layer between controller and repository. **Rejected**: The existing code doesn't have a service layer; controllers work directly with repositories. Introducing one would violate the constraint \"preserve existing architecture\" and create unrelated refactoring.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Caller receives | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|-----------------|-----------|\n| CREATED shipment | repository.findById() | repository.save() with status=CONFIRMED | Shipment with status=CONFIRMED, 200 OK | ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CONFIRMED shipment | repository.findById() | repository.save() with same data | Shipment unchanged, 200 OK | ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CANCELLED shipment | repository.findById() | (none) | ApiError with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED, 409 | throw ConflictException |\n| Non-existent ID | repository.findById() returns null | (none) | ApiError with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, 404 | throw ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Creates S-1, confirms it, verifies status changed to CONFIRMED and HTTP 200\n- Test 2: Creates S-2, confirms twice, verifies second confirm returns 200 with unchanged CONFIRMED status (idempotent)\n- Test 3: Directly saves S-3 with CANCELLED status in repository, attempts confirm, verifies 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED error code\n- Test 4: Attempts confirm on non-existent S-missing, verifies 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1028,"cache_read_input_tokens":20040,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1028},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1efd0d04-803d-40c1-8631-36655c1753b9","uuid":"547c8392-3fa6-4076-b8af-5068189b8936","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:05:01.085Z","request_id":"req_011CetJoWNCQ2qYukUtz8h7P"}
